+
+# Make applyPatch conform to RFC 6902 in every case, errors included
+
+## Request
+
+Users of `applyPatch` report invalid patches accepted, surprising edge-case results, and failures not
+behaving as RFC 6902 reads. Review how patches are checked and applied, and make the behaviour conform
+to RFC 6902 in every case, errors included.
+
+## Done
+
+- Reviewed `src/json-patch.ts` against RFC 6902 sections 3 to 5 and probed edge cases. The operation
+  semantics (add/remove/replace/move/copy/test, `-`, indices, move into a child, JSON equality,
+  atomicity) were found conforming; the defects were at the input boundary and in error reporting:
+  - a sparse patch skipped its holes (`[, op]` was applied as `[op]`);
+  - class instances and objects with an inherited `op` were accepted as operations;
+  - sparse arrays were accepted as JSON values;
+  - cyclic values, throwing getters/proxies and over-deep values escaped as raw `RangeError`/`TypeError`
+    instead of a `JsonPatchError` with `index`, `operation` and `cause`.
+- Fixed in `src/json-patch.ts` (indexed loop, plain-object and own-`op` checks, hole and cycle
+  detection in `cloneJson`, every failure wrapped as `JsonPatchError`); doc comment and `README.md`
+  updated.
+- `test/apply-patch.test.ts`: 7 tests added. Red first (5 failed before the fix): sparse patch,
+  non-plain operations, sparse arrays, cyclic value, error raised by a getter. Characterization (passed
+  on first run): non-JSON values and documents rejected; an object shared without a cycle accepted.
+  64 tests pass.
+- Decision: dl-004 (strict validation of patch and values, every failure a JsonPatchError).
+
+## Notes
+
+- dl-003 (the semantics of task-002) is still pending approval; dl-004 builds on it without changing
+  its decisions.
+- A valid document nested deeper than the call stack still fails (now as a `JsonPatchError`).
+- `tsc` is not installed, so type-checking was not run; no coverage threshold is declared.
